The Qwen3-TTS model code under Sources/VoiceMLX/ (talker, code predictor, 12 Hz
speech-tokenizer encoder and decoder, speaker encoder, configuration and weight
loading) started as copies of speech-swift Sources/Qwen3TTS/ and Sources/MLXCommon/
and was modified.

Prompt layouts, sampling semantics and the text tokenizer follow QwenLM's reference
implementation qwen-tts (https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-TTS, Apache License 2.0).

The SIM-o speaker-similarity scorer under Sources/SpeakerSim/ (WavLM-large +
ECAPA-TDNN) and the reference-transcript text helpers in Sources/VoiceAudio/TextPrep.swift
are ports of k2-fsa OmniVoice (https://github.com/k2-fsa/OmniVoice, Apache License 2.0;
omnivoice/eval/speaker_similarity and omnivoice/utils/text.py).

The resampler in Sources/VoiceAudio/Resampler.swift reproduces
torchaudio.functional.resample (BSD-2-Clause). The silence removal in
Sources/VoiceAudio/Silence.swift reproduces pydub (MIT) semantics.

Model weights are not part of this repository: the MLX bundles
aufklarer/Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-*-MLX-*, the codec Qwen/Qwen3-TTS-Tokenizer-12Hz and
the k2-fsa/TTS_eval_models speaker-similarity checkpoint are downloaded separately
and remain under their own licenses.
